# Design Execution

## Skill Routing — MANDATORY

When performing any design or UI task, you MUST load the relevant skills from `.cursor/skills/` (project) or `~/.cursor/skills/` (global) BEFORE generating code. Skills contain domain expertise that prevents generic output.

### Auto-Activate on ANY UI Generation

These skills fire on every UI generation task. Read them before writing code:

| Skill | Path | Trigger |
|-------|------|---------|
| **Design Taste Engine** | `.cursor/skills/design-taste-engine/SKILL.md` | ANY UI generation — building, designing, redesigning, improving, or creating interfaces, components, pages, dashboards, or applications. Provides mood, palette, typography pairing, spatial composition, and visual storytelling. |
| **Design Simulation Engine** | `.cursor/skills/design-simulation-engine/SKILL.md` | Every design task as the FIRST step before any visual decisions. Simulates human experience — predicts where eyes go, what the body feels, how the brain decides, and what they'll remember. |
| **Frontend Design (Anthropic)** | `~/.cursor/skills/frontend-design/SKILL.md` | ANY frontend UI generation — web components, pages, artifacts, landing pages, dashboards, React/HTML/CSS layouts. Anthropic's official skill for avoiding generic "AI slop" aesthetics. Pairs with Design Taste Engine: taste-engine sets the creative direction, frontend-design enforces craft discipline in the code. |
| **WCAG Accessibility** | `.cursor/skills/wcag-accessibility/SKILL.md` | Every UI generation task. WCAG 2.2 Level AA compliance — perceivable, operable, understandable, robust. |

